tml">Bayesian Inference</title><link href="/2019/07/07/bayesian-copy.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Bayesian Inference" /><published>2019-07-07T00:00:00-04:00</published><updated>2019-07-07T00:00:00-04:00</updated><id>/2019/07/07/bayesian%20copy</id><content type="html" xml:base="/2019/07/07/bayesian-copy.html">&lt;p&gt;This is a post about bayesian inference!&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Yuning Wu</name></author><summary type="html">This is a post about bayesian inference!</summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Bayesian Inference</title><link href="/2019/07/07/bayesian-copy-3.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Bayesian Inference" /><published>2019-07-07T00:00:00-04:00</published><updated>2019-07-07T00:00:00-04:00</updated><id>/2019/07/07/bayesian%20copy%203</id><content type="html" xml:base="/2019/07/07/bayesian-copy-3.html">&lt;p&gt;This is a post about bayesian inference!&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Yuning Wu</name></author><summary type="html">This is a post about bayesian inference!</summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE)</title><link href="/2018/08/20/test.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE)" /><published>2018-08-20T00:00:00-04:00</published><updated>2018-08-20T00:00:00-04:00</updated><id>/2018/08/20/test</id><content type="html" xml:base="/2018/08/20/test.html">&lt;p&gt;This is an introductory post about MLE.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1 id=&quot;measuring-difference-between-two-probability-distribution&quot;&gt;Measuring Difference Between Two Probability Distribution&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#measuring-difference-between-two-probability-distribution&quot;&gt;Measuring Difference Between Two Probability Distribution&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;ul&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#1-setting&quot;&gt;1. Setting&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
      &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#2measures&quot;&gt;2.Measures&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
          &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#21-total-variace&quot;&gt;2.1 Total Variace&lt;/a&gt;
            &lt;ul&gt;
              &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#211discreet--continuous-case&quot;&gt;2.1.1Discreet &amp;amp; continuous case&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
              &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#212-properties&quot;&gt;2.1.2 Properties&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
          &lt;/li&gt;
          &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#22-kullback-leibler-divergence&quot;&gt;2.2 Kullback-Leibler divergence&lt;/a&gt;
            &lt;ul&gt;
              &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#221-discreet--continuous-case&quot;&gt;2.2.1 Discreet &amp;amp; continuous case&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
              &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#222-property&quot;&gt;2.2.2 Property&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
              &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#223-kl-and-mle&quot;&gt;2.2.3 KL and MLE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
          &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
      &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;/ul&gt;
  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;1-setting&quot;&gt;1. Setting&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let ${E, (\mathbb{P}&lt;em&gt;{\theta})&lt;/em&gt;{\theta\in\Theta}}$ be a statistical model with a sample of $n$ i.i.d. r.v. $X_1, X_2, …, X_n$. Assume that $\theta^*\in\Theta$ is the true parameter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to find an estimator $\hat\theta=\hat\theta(X_1, X_2, …, X_n)$ s.t. $\mathbb{P}&lt;em&gt;{\theta}$ is close to $\mathbb{P}&lt;/em&gt;{\theta^&lt;em&gt;}$ for the true parameter $\theta^&lt;/em&gt;$&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This also means, 
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;\forall A\subset E, |\mathbb{P}_{\theta}(A) - \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}(A)|\text{ is small}&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;The two curves are as close as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;2measures&quot;&gt;2.Measures&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3 id=&quot;21-total-variace&quot;&gt;2.1 Total Variace&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex; mode=display&quot;&gt;TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})=\max_{A\subset E}|\mathbb{P}_{\theta}(A) - \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}(A)|&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;h4 id=&quot;211discreet--continuous-case&quot;&gt;2.1.1Discreet &amp;amp; continuous case&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})=\frac{1}{2}\sum\limits_{x\in E}|p_{\theta}(x) - p_{\theta^*}(x)|&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})=\frac{1}{2}\int\limits_{x\in E}|f_{\theta}(x) - f_{\theta^*}(x)|dx&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h4 id=&quot;212-properties&quot;&gt;2.1.2 Properties&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Symmetry. 
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})=TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta})&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Positive.
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;0 \leq TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})\leq 1&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Definite.
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})=0 \Longleftrightarrow \mathbb{P}_{\theta}= \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Triangle inequality.
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})\leq TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta'})+TV(\mathbb{P}_{\theta'}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Unclear how to build an estimator of TV from data.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;distance&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3 id=&quot;22-kullback-leibler-divergence&quot;&gt;2.2 Kullback-Leibler divergence&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h4 id=&quot;221-discreet--continuous-case&quot;&gt;2.2.1 Discreet &amp;amp; continuous case&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex; mode=display&quot;&gt;% &lt;![CDATA[
\begin{aligned}
KL(\mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta})&amp;=\sum\limits_{x \in E}p_{\theta^*}(x)\log\left(\frac{p_{\theta}(x)}{p_{\theta^*}(x)}\right)\\
&amp;=\mathbf{E}_{\theta}\left[\log\left(\frac{p_{\theta}(X)}{p_{\theta^*}(X)}\right)\right]\\
&amp;=\mathbf{E}\left[\log p_{\theta}(X)\right] - \mathbf{E}\left[\log p_{\theta^*}(X)\right]
\end{aligned} %]]&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex; mode=display&quot;&gt;% &lt;![CDATA[
\begin{aligned}
KL(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})&amp;=\int\limits_{x \in E}f_{\theta}(x)\log\left(\frac{f_{\theta}(x)}{f_{\theta^*}(x)}\right)dx\\
&amp;=\mathbf{E}\left[\log\left(\frac{f_{\theta}(X)}{f_{\theta^*}(X)}\right)\right]\\
&amp;=\mathbf{E}\left[\log f_{\theta}(X)\right] - \mathbf{E}\left[\log f_{\theta^*}(X)\right]
\end{aligned} %]]&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;h4 id=&quot;222-property&quot;&gt;2.2.2 Property&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Also known as relative entropy.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Not symmetric in general.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Positive.
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;KL(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}) \geq 0&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Definite.
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;KL(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})=0 \Longleftrightarrow \mathbb{P}_{\theta}= \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}&lt;/script&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;No triangle inequality.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;Not a &lt;strong&gt;distance&lt;/strong&gt;, a &lt;strong&gt;divergence&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;The asymmetry reflects a sense of &lt;strong&gt;suject&lt;/strong&gt;. For $KL(A, B)$, $A$ is the goal to reach and be compared with, whereas $B$ is the one the to compare.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h4 id=&quot;223-kl-and-mle&quot;&gt;2.2.3 KL and MLE&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider building an estimator $\widehat{KL}$ from $n$ i.i.d. r.v. $X_1, X_2, …, X_n$.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
  &lt;script type=&quot;math/tex; mode=display&quot;&gt;\mathbf{E}[const] = const&lt;/script&gt;

  &lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;The probability measure of $\mathbb{P}_{\theta}(X)$ is a r.v. because $\theta$ is a r.v.. There could be infinite kind of probability measures for $\theta\in\Theta$&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;The probability measure of $\mathbb{P}_{\theta^&lt;em&gt;}(X)$ is constant because $\theta^&lt;/em&gt;$ is constant.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Another way of thinking about this. $p_{\theta}(X)$ is a function of $(\theta, X)$. $\mathbf{E}[f(X, \theta)]$ is a function of only $\theta$. If $\theta$ is constant, then $\mathbf{E}[f(X, \theta)]$ is a constant.&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex; mode=display&quot;&gt;% &lt;![CDATA[
\begin{aligned}
KL(\mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta^*})
&amp;=\mathbf{E}_{\theta^*}[\log(p_{\theta^*}(X))] - \mathbf{E}_{\theta^*}[\log(p_{\theta}(X))]\\
&amp; = const - \mathbf{E}_{\theta^*}[\log(\mathbb{P}_{\theta}(X))]\\
\end{aligned} %]]&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let $Y=\log(\mathbb{P}&lt;em&gt;{\theta}(X))$. According to LLN, $\mathbf{E}&lt;/em&gt;{\theta^&lt;em&gt;}[Y]$ can be sampled by $\bar{Y}$
&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;% &lt;![CDATA[
\begin{aligned}
\widehat{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta})
&amp; = const - \frac{1}{n}\sum\limits_n\log\left(p_{\theta^*}(X_i)\right)\\
&amp; = const -\frac{1}{n}\log\left(\prod\limits_np_{\theta^*}(X_i)\right)\\
\end{aligned} %]]&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
Drawing $\theta$ closer to $\theta^&lt;/em&gt;$ is equivalent to &lt;strong&gt;minimizing&lt;/strong&gt; KL divergence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;script type=&quot;math/tex&quot;&gt;% &lt;![CDATA[
\begin{aligned}
    \min\limits_{\theta\in\Theta}\widehat{KL}(\mathbb{P}_{\theta^*}, \mathbb{P}_{\theta})&amp;\Leftrightarrow\min\limits_{\theta\in\Theta}-\frac{1}{n}\log\left(\prod\limits_np_{\theta^*}(X_i)\right)\\
    &amp;\Leftrightarrow\max\limits_{\theta\in\Theta}\frac{1}{n}\log\left(\prod\limits_np_{\theta^*}(X_i)\right)\\
    &amp;\Leftrightarrow\max\limits_{\theta\in\Theta}\prod\limits_np_{\theta^*}(X_i)\\
\end{aligned} %]]&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
Therefore, &lt;strong&gt;minimizing&lt;/strong&gt; KL divergence is equivalent to &lt;strong&gt;maximizing&lt;/strong&gt; likelihood.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Yuning Wu</name></author><summary type="html">This is an introductory post about MLE.</summary></entry></feed>